		<item>
			<title><![CDATA[Webring Manager]]></title>
			<link>https://playground.wordpress.net/webring-manager/</link>
			<pubDate>Tue, 07 Apr 2026 15:35:25 +0000</pubDate>
			<dc:creator><![CDATA[wapuu]]></dc:creator>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">https://playground.wordpress.net/?page_id=304</guid>
			<description></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The <strong>webring-manager</strong> plugin provides a set of flexible blocks to display and share members of your webring. This page explains how websites are organized and how each available block works.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Managing Webring Websites</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>All webring members are stored as a custom post type. You can manage them <a href="/wp-admin/edit.php?post_type=webring_website">in the WordPress dashboard</a> here.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Each entry represents a single website in a webring. When creating or editing a website, you can:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Set a title</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Set the website URL in the sidebar - <strong>this is important!</strong></li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Set a featured image (used in certain blocks)</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Assign categories</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These categories are especially important, as some blocks allow filtering based on them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Available Blocks</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Webring Website List</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This block works like the "Latest Posts" block and comes with two different view:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4,"fontSize":"large"} -->
<h4 class="wp-block-heading has-large-font-size">1. Grid View (with optional featured images)</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:webring-manager/website-list {"categories":[{"id":2,"name":"Blog"}],"postLayout":"grid","displayFeaturedImage":true,"featuredImageSizeSlug":"medium"} /-->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This block displays webring websites in a visual grid layout.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Optionally shows the <strong>featured image</strong> of each website</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Ideal for showcasing members in a more engaging, visual way</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Can be filtered by categories (e.g. only show websites in the <em>Blog</em> category)</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Use this block when you want to highlight your webring members prominently, especially if they provide good visuals.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":4,"fontSize":"large"} -->
<h4 class="wp-block-heading has-large-font-size">2. List View (without Featured Images)</h4>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:webring-manager/website-list {"categories":[{"id":3,"name":"Blog"}]} /-->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This block presents webring websites as a simple list.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>No featured images are displayed</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Focuses on titles and basic information</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>More compact and faster to scan</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is a good choice for minimal layouts or when you want a clean, text-focused overview of all members.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">HTML Snippet Block</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:webring-manager/html-snippet {"webringName":"DEWP Webring","showCustomizationInstructions":true,"enableSyntaxHighlighting":true,"syntaxHighlightingTheme":"prism-theme-okaidia"} /-->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This block outputs a ready-to-use HTML snippet.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Designed for embedding your webring on external sites</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Can be copied and shared with webring members</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item -->

	<!-- wp:list-item -->
	<li>Helps standardize how the webring is displayed across different websites</li>
	<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Use this block when you want to provide members with an easy way to link back to the webring.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Summary</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The webring-manager plugin separates <strong>content management</strong> (via the custom post type) from <strong>presentation</strong> (via blocks). This makes it easy to maintain your webring in one place while offering multiple display options depending on your needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Choose the grid for visual impact, the list for simplicity, and the HTML snippet for sharing your webring beyond your own site.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You’re ready to get started: head over <a href="/wp-admin/edit.php?post_type=webring_website">to the dashboard</a> at to add or update the webring members, assign categories, and upload featured images. If you’d like to see how everything comes together, <a href="/wp-admin/post.php?post=335&amp;action=edit">edit this page</a> in the block editor to explore how the different webring blocks are configured and displayed—you can easily adjust them to match your needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->]]></content:encoded>
